content.thinking:
`[role="tab"]:has-text("文件")` not found — the pane tab strip elements aren't role=tab. The screenshot showed 文件/预览 as text in the pane header. Use a plain text locator scoped to the pane: `:text("文件")` matches too many (body has 文件 in composer placeholder "发消息或创建任务, / 调用指令, @ 文件或对话"...). Need precision. Options:
- Scope to right pane container: the pane has class `_paneBody_...` (from the earlier DOM dump: SECTION._pane_11olo_209 at x1600, DIV._paneBody_11olo_312). CSS-module classes are hashed but stable within a build; risky.
- Use `:text("文件")` with .last() (pane is rightmost in DOM) — earlier probe2 used `page.locator('text=文件').last()` and it matched composer placeholder (placeholders are divs... the placeholder IS the last?). Composer is at page bottom in DOM, pane earlier? In probe2 the last() matched the placeholder.
- Better: find the tab strip by proximity: the pane tab strip sits at top of the pane — locator with position filter: `page.locator('span, button, div').filter({hasText:/^文件$/})` and pick the one with boundingBox y < 100 && x > 900.

Robust approach: evaluate DOM — find elements whose text is exactly 文件 with getBoundingClientRect, pick x>880. Use page.locator with a custom predicate via evaluateHandle... Simplest: use page.evaluate to find and click directly:

```js
await page.evaluate(() => {
  const els=[...document.querySelectorAll('*')].filter(e=>e.children.length===0 && e.textContent?.trim()==='文件');
  const el=els.find(e=>{const r=e.getBoundingClientRect();return r.x>880&&r.y<100&&r.width>0});
  el?.closest('[role="tab"],button,a,[class]')?.click() || el?.click();
});
```

Click the leaf text element; React onClick is on the parent tab button — clicking the child bubbles ✓.

Also after switching to 文件 tab, tree loads; then click spike-doc.plate row.

Patch the probe with this evaluate-based click.

