Server side is PERFECT: plate_open created the doc (seq 0), then TWO plate_edit calls landed (seq 2, cause 'ai') with proper content (h1 title, h2 heading, paragraphs — the agent followed the guide!). The agent chain works end-to-end.

The problem is purely CLIENT-side: PlateLivePage fetched doc-open ONCE at mount (when the doc was empty), and never re-fetches — so the editor shows empty content while the server has 1695 chars. Confirmed my hypothesis.

Fix: live refresh in PlateLivePage:
- Poll doc-open every ~2.5s while the tab exists.
- When head.slateJson JSON differs from the last-rendered head AND the user isn't actively editing inside the editor (document.activeElement not within .plate-live-page), update state with the new content + revision key → remount PlateDocEditor with key={revision} so the new content renders.
- If the user IS actively typing, skip the refresh (protect local edits; v1 honest limitation — like office's HUMAN_EDITING pause).

Implementation in PlateLivePage:
```tsx
const [state, setState] = useState<{ docId: string; title: string; content: SlateContent; revision: number } | null>(null);
const renderedRef = useRef(''); // JSON of last rendered content

// initial load (existing effect) + poll loop
useEffect(() => {
  if (!docId) return;
  let cancelled = false;
  const load = async () => {
    try {
      const result = await post(... doc-open ...);
      if (cancelled) return;
      const headJson = JSON.stringify(result.head.slateJson);
      if (headJson !== renderedRef.current) {
        const editing = document.activeElement && document.querySelector('.plate-live-page')?.contains(document.activeElement);
        if (!editing) {
          renderedRef.current = headJson;
          setState({ docId, title: result.doc.title, content: result.head.slateJson, revision: result.head.seq });
        }
      }
    } catch { /* 文档尚未提交或服务暂不可用 */ }
    finally { if (!cancelled) setBusy(false); }
  };
  void load();
  const timer = setInterval(() => void load(), 2500);
  return () => { cancelled = true; clearInterval(timer); };
}, [docId]);
```
Wait — busy flag: initial load sets busy true until first load; subsequent polls shouldn't flip busy. Restructure: keep initial-load effect for busy, add a separate poll effect. Simpler: one effect; busy only until first successful/failed load (track with a ref or state flag).

Also: remount via key — `<PlateDocEditor key={state.revision} ... />`. When AI commits while user not editing → remount with fresh content. Caret loss only when not focused (guard).

Also update the E2E probe: the content should appear within ~2 polls after plate_edit commits. The 300s window should now capture it.

Note the doc already has content — after client fix deploy, the SAME doc will show content when the tab opens (proves refresh works even for the mount case).

Also add the state.reset on docId change (existing setState(null)).

One more consideration — the poll makes a request every 2.5s per mounted tab. Fine locally.

Implement now: edit client.tsx PlateLivePage. Also bump to 1.3.2 (another deploy cycle). Then re-run E2E (content should appear).

