1. `Sidebar Session opening failed: Session reference "..." is released` — the known session-adoption flakiness.
2. **`Plate hooks must be used inside a Plate or PlateController`** — at `usePlateStore` — and "slot entry crashed in 'sidebar.right.pane.tab'".

That's a REAL crash I introduced! `useEditorVersion()` calls `usePlateStore(...)` which requires being inside a `<Plate>` or `PlateController`. In `PlateDocEditor`, I call `useEditorVersion()` at the top of the component — but `<Plate editor={editor}>` is rendered INSIDE that component's JSX. So `PlateDocEditor` itself is NOT inside a Plate context — only its children are. Hence the crash.

That's exactly the trap recorded in memory: 「工具栏必须嵌在 <Plate> 子树 + useEditorVersion() 订阅」 — the toolbar is a child inside `<Plate>`. I put it in the parent.

Fix: move the live-fingerprint sync into a child component rendered inside `<Plate>`. The toolbar (`PlateToolbarButtons`) is already inside. But the sync needs to run on every editor change — a tiny component inside `<Plate>` that does `useEditorVersion()` + assigns to the ref.

